From: MedveTalkie integration
Subject: [PATCH] unisocwifi: prepare ADDBA before queueing the data frame

sprdwl_tx_msg_func() called prepare_addba(intf, dscr->sta_lut_index,
msg->skb, peer_entry, tid) after the message had been queued, and outside
the data/QoS branch:

- For data frames, sprdwl_queue_data_msg_buf() hands msg to the TX thread,
  which may send and free the skb that holds dscr before prepare_addba()
  reads dscr->sta_lut_index and skb->data. That is a use-after-free under
  load.
- For command buffers, peer_entry is NULL so no ADDBA is sent, but the
  condition first reads intf->tx_num[lut_index] with a "LUT index" taken
  from the command payload. That is an out-of-bounds read of the 32-entry
  array.

Call prepare_addba() inside the data/QoS branch, before the queue becomes visible to the TX worker, while dscr, skb, peer_entry and tid are
still owned by this function. Move the mode queue counter increment before
handoff as well, avoiding another post-enqueue read of msg->mode.

For the same reason, read msg->msg_type into a local before queueing and
use it for the tx_up() decisions after the enqueue.

---
diff --git a/unisocwifi/tx_msg.c b/unisocwifi/tx_msg.c
index 7bb3e8b..2ded243 100644
--- a/unisocwifi/tx_msg.c
+++ b/unisocwifi/tx_msg.c
@@ -1241,6 +1241,8 @@ int sprdwl_tx_msg_func(void *pdev, struct sprdwl_msg_buf *msg)
 	struct sprdwl_peer_entry *peer_entry = NULL;
 	unsigned char tid = 0, tos = 0;
 	struct tx_msdu_dscr *dscr = (struct tx_msdu_dscr *)msg->tran_data;
+	/* msg belongs to the TX thread once queued: keep what we need */
+	int msg_type = msg->msg_type;
 
 	if (msg->msglist == &tx_msg->tx_list_cmd) {
 		len = SPRDWL_MAX_CMD_TXLEN;
@@ -1300,5 +1302,10 @@ int sprdwl_tx_msg_func(void *pdev, struct sprdwl_msg_buf *msg)
 			) {*/
 			msg->data_list = data_list;
+			/* Descriptor/SKB may be freed once queued. Do this first. */
+			prepare_addba(intf, dscr->sta_lut_index,
+				      (struct sk_buff *)msg->skb, peer_entry, tid);
+			/* Publish count before the TX worker can dequeue the buffer. */
+			atomic_inc(&tx_msg->tx_list[msg->mode]->mode_list_num);
 			sprdwl_queue_data_msg_buf(msg);
-			atomic_inc(&tx_msg->tx_list[msg->mode]->mode_list_num);
 		/*} else {
@@ -1331,15 +1336,12 @@ int sprdwl_tx_msg_func(void *pdev, struct sprdwl_msg_buf *msg)
 		}*/
 	}
 
-	if (msg->msg_type != SPRDWL_TYPE_DATA)
+	if (msg_type != SPRDWL_TYPE_DATA)
 		sprdwl_queue_msg_buf(msg, msg->msglist);
 
-	prepare_addba(intf, dscr->sta_lut_index, (struct sk_buff *)msg->skb,
-			 peer_entry, tid);
-
-	if (msg->msg_type == SPRDWL_TYPE_CMD)
+	if (msg_type == SPRDWL_TYPE_CMD)
 		tx_up(tx_msg);
-	if (msg->msg_type == SPRDWL_TYPE_DATA &&
+	if (msg_type == SPRDWL_TYPE_DATA &&
 		((intf->fw_awake == 0 &&
 		intf->fw_power_down == 1) ||
 		intf->fw_awake == 1))
